 7 | struct Undescribable;
   | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   = note: axum-oas refuses to silently omit a handler's response from the generated spec (compile-error over silent omission)
   = note: return `axum::Json<T>` or a typed response like `axum_oas::Ok<T>`, `axum_oas::Created<T>`, or `axum_oas::NoContent`, with `T` deriving `schemars::JsonSchema`
   = note: or implement `axum_oas::OperationOutput` for `Undescribable` to declare its status codes and body schema yourself
   = help: the following other types implement trait `OperationOutput`:
             Created<T>
             Json<T>
             Result<T, E>
             axum_oas::NoContent
             axum_oas::Ok<T>
   = note: required for `fn() -> impl Future<Output = Undescribable> {handler}` to implement `OasHandler<((),), _>`
